                                "sense_id": "598c11c1-cace-33e5-bcea-c5eb9fc6a6ba",
                                "text": "1997, Neil W. Hamilton (quoting Owen Lattimore), Zealotry and Academic Freedom, page 313,\nThis commonplace observation becomes very poignant when you are the man accused, and a man like McCarthy ruthfully exploits his advantage by making the accusations so sensational that the revelation of the truth seems drab and dull by comparison."
